# Fault W-E1-F1: the joint merge renamed a member's id even where the same word is a word of the language: an index
# named `month` (`index month = month ...`), a def named `value` (a built-in name), ids named like record fields
# (`amount`, `day`): LOAD-PARSE or LOAD-FIELD when joined, fine alone. L §2.2: built-in names are built-ins "only
# directly before `(`", contextual words "are reserved only in their own position, and are free everywhere else"; L
# §6.1 a member is read as when it loads alone. The member alone gives (1, 1, 3.00 DUK, 7.00 DUK) (q0, an ask of the
# member, not asked here); the joint model reads the same values under the prefix a (q): w is 1, value is 1, pay moves
# amount = 3.00 DUK out of x, which opens at 10.00 DUK.
=== options pin=bytes
=== f1j.tally
model j
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-01-31
  use a = "f1m.tally" sha256 "da930679075d6aedcdf58b52a89ab9ea46eedd8a69e239fc19ceecdc028db907"

ask q: a.w[2026-02], a.value, a.paid[2026-01], bal(a.x, 2026-01-31)
=== f1m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-01-31

unit DUK: currency minor 0.01
source s "s"

index month = month 2026-01..2026-03

def w[k in month]: int = 1
def value: int = 1
input amount: money DUK
input day: date
place x: accounts DUK lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 2026-01-01..
move pay: transfers
  on day
  leg cash from x to world amount amount
def paid[k in month]: money DUK = sum(t.cash.amount for t in transfers over k)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  amount = 3.00 DUK "a"
  day = 2026-01-10 "d"
  opening[x] = 10.00 DUK at 2026-01-01 start "o"

ask q0: w[2026-02], value, paid[2026-01], bal(x, 2026-01-31)
=== expect
q: (1, 1, 3.00 DUK, 7.00 DUK)
  unfulfilled: a.pay
  cut 2026-01-31
